A||N||4||Seanh||All Smokin and no power! Need some help.||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||05-08-2001||08:09 PM||||Well, I was driving the 87 GT, V6 auto, to school today and after school went to a friends house. He'd never seen this car before, so we were lookin over the engine and all. I got it and fired it up and reved it a couple of times, not excessively hard, and he walks up to the window and asked if my car always smoked this much. I said it usally doesn't smoke at all. I went to look and wow, it was pouring out smoke like you wouldn't believe. Worse when you rev it a little. I shut it off to look at the engine for an obvious problem and found nothing. I started it up again and it wouldn't start. I kept crankin and after about 10 seconds of solid crank time, it fired up and started running. Still smoking like crazy, but running. Took it for a short drive and it idles ok, but has a loss of power and smokes like crazy. It looks like a fairly white smoke, at times a little dark but not "black" smoke. Any ideas on what to check? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-08-2001||08:33 PM||||Compression test time.... sounds like the head gasket poped.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||05-08-2001||10:34 PM||||Oh no, not ANOTHER head gasket. What is it with me and head gaskets? I'll check on it tomarrow.<P>How long SHOULD it take a normal automotivly inclined person to change head gaskets? I took my own sweet time last time since the car wouldn't be driven in winter anyway. Could it be done in a weekend? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||05-10-2001||09:47 PM||||Oh thank god! It itsn't the head gaskets! Apperantly one of the fuel injectors crapped out on me. I was in a hurry so I just bought a new setup from NAPA, and the car runs great again. Wheww!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-11-2001||01:09 PM||||Facinating Spock<BR>The dead cylinder must have been sucking up oil and pumping it out ||||reg||1
